
# Team Working Agreement and Definition of Done

## 1. Overview
This document establishes the team's working agreement, responsibilities, and Definition of Done to ensure organized collaboration and consistent project development.

## 2. Communication and Collaboration Rules
- Communicate respectfully with all team members.
- Provide regular updates about assigned tasks.
- Inform the team about problems or delays.
- Participate in meetings and team discussions.
- Help other members when assistance is needed.
- Keep project-related communication clear and organized.

## 3. Team Roles and Responsibilities
- Project Leader: Monitors progress and coordinates team activities.
- Scrum Master: Helps organize sprint activities and addresses impediments.
- Developers: Work on assigned tasks and contribute to project development.
- Documentation Team: Maintains project records and technical documentation.
- Testers: Check completed features and report errors or issues.

## 4. Definition of Done
A task is considered complete when:
- The assigned requirements have been fulfilled.
- The work has been properly tested or reviewed.
- No major errors remain unresolved.
- Documentation is updated when necessary.
- Changes are committed and pushed to the correct GitHub branch.
- A pull request has been submitted for review.
- Required approvals have been received.

## 5. Team Commitment
Every member is expected to fulfill their responsibilities, meet agreed deadlines, communicate progress, and contribute to achieving the team's sprint goals.

## 6. Conclusion
This working agreement provides clear guidelines for teamwork, communication, and task completion. Following these standards will help maintain productivity, accountability, and consistency throughout the project.
